@meta
id: 05-03
title: The end of a word
chapter: 05
type: lesson
skills: word-e, word-w
par: 16
minutes: 4
vscode: double-click the word, then click either end of the selection
open: api.md

@brief
`w` and `b` both land on the *start* of a word. Half the time what you
want is the other end — you are adding a suffix, a closing quote, a
question mark. Vim has a motion for that too.

In this doc, `cancel` is a mutation name and should be in backticks:

    Call the `cancel` mutation with the order id.

One backtick goes in front of the word and one after it. Do both without
moving a character at a time and without touching the rest of the line.

@keys
| `e` | forward to the end of the current or next word |
| `w` | forward to the start of the next word |
| `i` | insert before the cursor |
| `a` | insert after the cursor |

@hints
Two inserts, at two different ends of the same word. `w` gets you to the
front. Something else gets you to the back.
--
`e` moves to the last character of a word. `a` then appends after the
character you are sitting on, so `ea` is "start typing at the end of this
word".
--
`ww` lands on `cancel`, `i` and a backtick puts one in front. `Esc` drops
you back on that new backtick; `e` now runs to the end of `cancel`, and
`a` with a backtick closes it.

@solution
    ww  i`<Esc>  e  a`<Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Two motions, two one-character inserts, thirteen keystrokes including the
save. The mouse route is double-click, type a backtick, watch the
selection vanish, click again at the other end, type another.

The pattern worth memorising is the pairing:

    w  then  i     insert in front of a word
    e  then  a     append to the end of a word

`ea` is how you pluralise an identifier, add a `?` to a field, or close a
quote. It will come up constantly.

One detail that saves confusion later: `e` from the middle of a word goes
to the end of *that* word, not the next one. It only moves on to the next
word if you are already sitting on the last character.

@start api.md
Call the cancel mutation with the order id. It returns the updated order.

@expected api.md
Call the `cancel` mutation with the order id. It returns the updated order.
